  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Afrobarometer Round 5-6 2011-17 - Afrobarometer Round five 2011-17</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Afrobarometer Round 5-6 2011-17</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">AfroBarometern (AB) &#xe4;r en serie av unders&#xf6;kningar av allm&#xe4;nhetens     inst&#xe4;llningar till demokrati, marknader och civilsamh&#xe4;llet i Afrika.  AB skall impl. i ett 30-35 Afr. l&#xe4;nder. Exempel p&#xe5; m&#xe5;l med programmet &#xe4;r att &#xf6;ka ABs synbarhet bland politiska akt&#xf6;rer och att forts&#xe4;tta    bygga institutionell kapacitet f&#xf6;r vetenskaplig forskning.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Afrobarometer (AB) is a series of gallups assessing popular       perceptions concerning democracy, markets, and civil society in       Africa. AB intends to implement its program in 30-35 African          countries. Exampel of objective with the programme is to increase AB  visibility amongst political actors and to continue building inst.    capacity of scientific reasearch.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overarching objective of Afrobarometer (AB) is African citizens&apos; opinions about democracy and development are heard and made part of the public policy debate while the following overall objectives were set out in the recently finalized phase of the program;
&#x2022; To expand coverage to 35 countries &#x2022; To enhance the visibility of the Afrobarometer among African Policy Actors through professionalization of the Afrobarometer&#x2019;s Communications Program, prioritizing the timeliness, accessibility and continuity in the release of results, and building ongoing engagement with stakeholders. &#x2022; To continue building Institutional Capacity for survey research and scientific analysis in Africa. &#x2022; To continue strengthening and indigenizing Network Management.</narrative>
  </description>
